WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:03.180
- What?
(quiet yay)

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.920
(cute electronic music)
- Whatcha got there?

00:00:17.872 --> 00:00:20.709
Hello, darling humans, I'm Hannah,

00:00:20.709 --> 00:00:22.299
and I haven't quite figured out

00:00:22.299 --> 00:00:24.194
what I'm gonna do to intro this.

00:00:24.194 --> 00:00:25.919
But in the last couple
of videos we've done,

00:00:25.919 --> 00:00:28.125
we post a number that you guys can text me

00:00:28.125 --> 00:00:30.538
to say any ideas that you
have for future episodes,

00:00:30.538 --> 00:00:32.413
and it was very clear
what you guys wanted,

00:00:32.413 --> 00:00:33.961
and so we're gonna give it to you today.

00:00:33.961 --> 00:00:36.930
I let my kids dress me for a whole week.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:40.128
It was very fun, it was very
weird, and I learned a lot.

00:00:40.128 --> 00:00:42.797
So first, as always, I needed
to lay some ground rules,

00:00:42.797 --> 00:00:45.167
most importantly so I
didn't get arrested in this

00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:48.059
experiment for, like, public
indecency or something.

00:00:48.059 --> 00:00:50.149
First rule was I needed
to be fully clothed.

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:53.046
There was going to be no
underwear in place of pants,

00:00:53.046 --> 00:00:55.691
or bathing suit tops in place of shirts,

00:00:55.691 --> 00:00:57.818
or underwear on my head as a hat.

00:00:57.818 --> 00:01:00.593
Because I have two boys,
they think it's very funny.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.371
So second, I tried to give them

00:01:02.371 --> 00:01:04.769
equal opportunity to each choose an outfit

00:01:04.769 --> 00:01:06.672
for those of you who understand

00:01:06.672 --> 00:01:08.181
what life is like with two boys.

00:01:08.181 --> 00:01:11.356
There's a lot of conflict around sharing,

00:01:11.356 --> 00:01:13.467
so I just straight up delegated days

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.774
to each kid so that it
wasn't an hour of them

00:01:15.774 --> 00:01:17.910
like, arguing over who got to pick what.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.478
And third, I had to do
this for seven days,

00:01:20.478 --> 00:01:24.279
and I had to follow through
with whatever outfit they chose,

00:01:24.279 --> 00:01:26.600
within reason, and I
immediately regretted that.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:27.565
(laughs)

00:01:27.565 --> 00:01:31.648
Day one of these boys
picking out my clothes.

00:01:31.648 --> 00:01:34.360
So day one, I decided
Jaxon would pick my outfit

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.074
because he's pretty stylish, he likes to

00:01:36.074 --> 00:01:37.410
dress himself, he kind of knows

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.406
how to coordinate outfits, and that day,

00:01:39.406 --> 00:01:40.727
I happened to have a friend in town

00:01:40.727 --> 00:01:42.420
who was visiting and so I was taking her

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.336
to the Getty Villa in Malibu, and we were

00:01:45.336 --> 00:01:47.129
gonna be around a lot of people

00:01:47.129 --> 00:01:48.950
because it's a big tourist attraction.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:50.909
So right off the bat, he picks the top,

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:52.723
and he chooses this off the shoulder

00:01:52.723 --> 00:01:56.930
kind of billowy, flowy,
pink and black tie-dyed top

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:59.256
that I actually just
bought recently and I love.

00:01:59.256 --> 00:02:01.158
That shirt? Okay.

00:02:01.158 --> 00:02:03.395
What he chose for the bottoms were

00:02:03.395 --> 00:02:07.694
these children's Old
Navy size large shorts

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:10.212
that I'd gotten at a
children's thrift store

00:02:10.212 --> 00:02:13.310
and they are baby blue
with white polka dots.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:15.253
Oh my God.
- Now get dressed!

00:02:15.253 --> 00:02:16.819
(Hannah laughs)

00:02:16.819 --> 00:02:18.932
- I looked like a spotted, deranged

00:02:18.932 --> 00:02:20.736
Oompa Loompa in this outfit.

00:02:20.736 --> 00:02:23.141
I keep forgetting that I'm wearing this

00:02:23.141 --> 00:02:25.213
and people keep staring at me and I think

00:02:25.213 --> 00:02:26.598
that they're staring at my hair

00:02:26.598 --> 00:02:30.106
and then I realize it's ...
just this.

00:02:30.106 --> 00:02:31.403
(her friend giggles)

00:02:31.403 --> 00:02:33.878
Let me tell you no one was
looking at the art that day.

00:02:33.878 --> 00:02:35.380
They were looking at my outfit.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.267
That was a pretty ridiculous way

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:38.697
to start out the experiment.

00:02:38.697 --> 00:02:40.211
It was kind of like my worst fears

00:02:40.211 --> 00:02:42.523
all coming true on day one.

00:02:42.523 --> 00:02:45.741
So, day two, I gave Jaxon
a chance to redeem himself.

00:02:45.741 --> 00:02:48.460
We needed a do-over, so
he chose a really cute

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:51.391
romper that I love and actually gave me

00:02:51.391 --> 00:02:52.874
a hoodie to wear too, which I was

00:02:52.874 --> 00:02:55.167
excited about because it
was chilly out that day.

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:56.630
So I left the house feeling very happy

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:59.459
in my cute romper until
I remembered one thing.

00:02:59.459 --> 00:03:00.938
I totally forgot that today I have

00:03:00.938 --> 00:03:03.025
a doctor's appointment, and TMI,

00:03:03.025 --> 00:03:05.857
but it's a female doctor's appointment

00:03:05.857 --> 00:03:08.858
where you have to undress
from the waist down.

00:03:08.858 --> 00:03:10.778
You girls out there know the struggle

00:03:10.778 --> 00:03:13.035
of trying to, like, pee in a romper.

00:03:13.035 --> 00:03:15.038
You have to just take everything off

00:03:15.038 --> 00:03:17.434
and like get completely
naked in the stall.

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:20.544
I was about to have to do
that in the doctor's office.

00:03:20.544 --> 00:03:22.505
So I have a t-shirt that I'm gonna bring

00:03:22.505 --> 00:03:25.456
into the office to change when they

00:03:25.456 --> 00:03:28.890
ask me to take my clothes
off from the waist down.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.256
And as if it's not awkward enough

00:03:30.256 --> 00:03:31.821
to go to like the lady doctor,

00:03:31.821 --> 00:03:34.011
it would've been so much more awkward

00:03:34.011 --> 00:03:35.314
if she came back in the room and

00:03:35.314 --> 00:03:37.498
I was like, "Hey, it's me, naked."

00:03:37.498 --> 00:03:40.102
So day two, you know,
it was a cute outfit.

00:03:40.102 --> 00:03:41.945
It's just when you're having someone else

00:03:41.945 --> 00:03:43.598
pick out your clothes,
they're not thinking

00:03:43.598 --> 00:03:45.047
of what your day is going to be,

00:03:45.047 --> 00:03:46.589
especially when they're five years old.

00:03:46.589 --> 00:03:48.946
So day three, Jaxon's choice once again.

00:03:48.946 --> 00:03:51.040
I think he was in kind of a weird mood

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:54.171
because he chose this random t-shirt

00:03:54.171 --> 00:03:56.152
for me to wear, and it's
like a yellow t-shirt

00:03:56.152 --> 00:03:58.176
with a girl on a motorcycle, and it says

00:03:58.176 --> 00:04:01.872
Motorcycle: put something
exciting between your legs.

00:04:01.872 --> 00:04:03.135
He doesn't know how to read!

00:04:03.135 --> 00:04:04.748
And then he chose these kinda silly

00:04:04.748 --> 00:04:07.282
floral shorts to pair with it.

00:04:07.282 --> 00:04:09.533
- This is what you should wear.

00:04:09.533 --> 00:04:11.116
- Those? All right.

00:04:12.512 --> 00:04:14.225
We don't have much of
a dress code at work,

00:04:14.225 --> 00:04:15.730
and it's pretty casual because it's

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:17.182
a creative environment and we're allowed

00:04:17.182 --> 00:04:19.229
to kind of like wear
what makes us comfortable

00:04:19.229 --> 00:04:21.275
but this was just like, I felt weird

00:04:21.275 --> 00:04:23.200
walking in the door, but luckily,

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.406
that day, Jaxon was
coming to work with me,

00:04:25.406 --> 00:04:28.663
and he decided, for
himself, he wanted to wear

00:04:28.663 --> 00:04:32.266
some Halloween costume
werewolf hands to work with me.

00:04:32.266 --> 00:04:33.713
I got a weird kid, what can I say.

00:04:33.713 --> 00:04:36.634
So at least we looked ridiculous together.

00:04:36.634 --> 00:04:38.915
Rolling up on day four, I don't know

00:04:38.915 --> 00:04:42.175
what to expect at this point,
it was Wyatt's choice today.

00:04:42.175 --> 00:04:43.999
So first he tried to choose the romper

00:04:43.999 --> 00:04:45.886
that I'd already worn, but I vetoed that

00:04:45.886 --> 00:04:47.790
because I figured this experiment

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:50.064
is best with seven separate outfits.

00:04:50.064 --> 00:04:52.200
So instead, he chose a jumpsuit

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.534
that I bought on sale
online without trying on

00:04:55.534 --> 00:04:57.425
and then it arrived and it fit,

00:04:57.425 --> 00:04:59.365
then the second I washed it, it shrank,

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:01.834
and it was like way too tight.
Way too tight!

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.637
Since it was really tight, if I wore

00:05:03.637 --> 00:05:06.637
any underwear under it, it would've shown.

00:05:06.637 --> 00:05:08.716
So I had no choice but to go commando

00:05:08.716 --> 00:05:11.539
and with that being said,
I had to tie a sweater

00:05:11.539 --> 00:05:15.121
around my waist to avoid
any cameltoe mishaps,

00:05:15.121 --> 00:05:17.085
'cause I was going to work in this.

00:05:17.085 --> 00:05:19.870
Leave it to Wyatt to almost make me expose

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:22.977
all of my parts to everybody at work.

00:05:22.977 --> 00:05:25.012
So day five was finally the first

00:05:25.012 --> 00:05:27.549
collaborative effort between both kids,

00:05:27.549 --> 00:05:29.482
and they actually ended
up dressing me head to toe

00:05:29.482 --> 00:05:31.233
because they got so involved in this,

00:05:31.233 --> 00:05:32.978
they decided they had to pick my shoes.

00:05:32.978 --> 00:05:34.895
So Jaxon and Wyatt collectively chose

00:05:34.895 --> 00:05:36.613
this really beautiful blue dress

00:05:36.613 --> 00:05:38.716
that I really enjoy wearing and then

00:05:38.716 --> 00:05:42.883
Jaxon just had to pull out
some sort of wild card.

00:05:44.257 --> 00:05:46.100
- These I want you to wear.

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:48.613
- That dress and my PJ shorts.

00:05:48.613 --> 00:05:52.110
According to Jaxon, you can't
wear a dress without bottoms.

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:53.343
Don't know where he's getting these

00:05:53.343 --> 00:05:55.101
fashion rules, but he ended up choosing

00:05:55.101 --> 00:05:58.316
the most bulky pair of pajama shorts I own

00:05:58.316 --> 00:05:59.610
for me to wear under it.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:02.284
It was a very bulky day.
Very bulky day.

00:06:02.284 --> 00:06:03.828
How do you like my outfit, Jaxon?

00:06:03.828 --> 00:06:05.184
Do you still like it?
- Good.

00:06:05.184 --> 00:06:07.292
- Good?
Let's see what Daddy thinks.

00:06:07.292 --> 00:06:10.292
Dee, what do you think of my outfit?

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:13.954
- I love it.

00:06:13.954 --> 00:06:16.508
- So day six, almost at the end,

00:06:16.508 --> 00:06:20.112
and day six was straight
up Wyatt's time to shine.

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:22.463
And I think he had
spent the past five days

00:06:22.463 --> 00:06:24.189
really thinking about what he wanted

00:06:24.189 --> 00:06:25.817
because the second I told him he could

00:06:25.817 --> 00:06:27.638
choose my outfit, he just bolted

00:06:27.638 --> 00:06:31.086
to this random knit poncho that I've had

00:06:31.086 --> 00:06:33.033
hanging in my closet for years.

00:06:33.033 --> 00:06:34.033
This?
- This.

00:06:35.575 --> 00:06:37.158
- This poncho?
Okay.

00:06:39.978 --> 00:06:41.333
Oh yeah, jump on it, and make sure

00:06:41.333 --> 00:06:44.273
it's nice and worn in, right?

00:06:44.273 --> 00:06:47.630
He ends up deciding on some
denim cutoffs to pair with it.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:51.070
I looked like I was ready for
an evening Coachella show.

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:52.984
Whoo-hoo, Coachella!

00:06:52.984 --> 00:06:55.551
My kids are gonna look
back on this and watch it

00:06:55.551 --> 00:06:58.149
and be like, holy crap,
Mom, you're embarrassing.

00:06:58.149 --> 00:07:01.318
- Kendrick Lamar on the main stage!

00:07:01.318 --> 00:07:04.762
I just realized that this whole experiment

00:07:04.762 --> 00:07:07.557
with having my kids dress me has forced me

00:07:07.557 --> 00:07:09.781
to wake up a lot earlier because usually

00:07:09.781 --> 00:07:11.779
I just like throw on whatever the first

00:07:11.779 --> 00:07:13.905
thing I grab is, out
of my closet, but they

00:07:13.905 --> 00:07:16.860
actually like to take their
time choosing my outfits,

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:20.544
so I'm exhausted, I'm really tired.

00:07:20.544 --> 00:07:23.172
So day seven, the grand finale.

00:07:23.172 --> 00:07:25.470
I decided that I wanted you guys

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:27.415
to experience this with me live,

00:07:27.415 --> 00:07:29.635
so today is actually my day seven outfit.

00:07:29.635 --> 00:07:32.294
It is brought to you 100% by Jaxon.

00:07:32.294 --> 00:07:34.237
He dressed me head to toe this time,

00:07:34.237 --> 00:07:36.720
and I think he kinda wanted
to go out with a bang

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:38.273
because he was very adamant about

00:07:38.273 --> 00:07:39.575
picking something a little more

00:07:39.575 --> 00:07:40.900
formal for me and kept saying,

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:43.005
"Mom, you gotta look nice,
you gotta look nice."

00:07:43.005 --> 00:07:46.756
and today, I got a lot of
compliments from my coworkers.

00:07:46.756 --> 00:07:49.412
- Oh, damn, Hannah.
- [Hannah] What?

00:07:49.412 --> 00:07:51.197
- You look super cute.

00:07:51.197 --> 00:07:54.470
I don't know if I just
generally dress crappy

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:57.069
or if this past week
has been so ridiculous.

00:07:57.069 --> 00:07:58.791
You know, Jaxon dressed me.

00:07:58.791 --> 00:08:00.083
(happy squeal)

00:08:00.083 --> 00:08:03.925
- Oh my God, can he dress me?
(laughing) He's styling.

00:08:03.925 --> 00:08:06.832
- So after a week of like
really all over the place

00:08:06.832 --> 00:08:09.970
outfits, real hit and
misses, Jaxon comes through

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:14.137
on day seven, and I feel
really good about myself.

00:08:15.551 --> 00:08:18.479
I don't know how to model.

00:08:18.479 --> 00:08:21.075
What do you do with your hands?

00:08:21.075 --> 00:08:23.234
So what did I learn this week?

00:08:23.234 --> 00:08:24.782
Well, I actually learned a whole lot more

00:08:24.782 --> 00:08:26.118
than I thought I would.

00:08:26.118 --> 00:08:29.273
First and foremost, I need
to clean out my dang closet.

00:08:29.273 --> 00:08:31.661
The fact that these items like the poncho,

00:08:31.661 --> 00:08:34.612
the jumpsuit, and the polka dot shorts

00:08:34.612 --> 00:08:37.332
were in my closet and in my drawers,

00:08:37.332 --> 00:08:38.986
that's on me, that's my fault.

00:08:38.986 --> 00:08:40.571
The second thing I learned is that I could

00:08:40.571 --> 00:08:43.506
afford to spend some more
time choosing my outfits.

00:08:43.506 --> 00:08:45.323
I think a lot of you moms
out there can also relate.

00:08:45.323 --> 00:08:47.691
The morning is mostly spent making sure

00:08:47.691 --> 00:08:49.928
that my children are
fully clothed and dressed

00:08:49.928 --> 00:08:52.494
and then I'm kind of an afterthought,

00:08:52.494 --> 00:08:55.932
but I realized I go to work, I see people,

00:08:55.932 --> 00:08:57.462
I need to look presentable.

00:08:57.462 --> 00:08:59.980
So it's important for me to
spend some time on myself

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:01.588
and my outfit and make sure that

00:09:01.588 --> 00:09:03.809
I feel confident and look nice.

00:09:03.809 --> 00:09:05.865
And the final thing I learned is that

00:09:05.865 --> 00:09:08.316
I don't give a crap
what anyone else thinks,

00:09:08.316 --> 00:09:10.148
and that is something that I've noticed--

00:09:10.148 --> 00:09:12.070
(bird caws)
Hello.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.736
And the thing thing that I learned

00:09:13.736 --> 00:09:16.617
is that I don't give a crap
what anyone else thinks of me.

00:09:16.617 --> 00:09:17.805
(bird caws)
What?!

00:09:17.805 --> 00:09:19.481
And this is something that I've realized

00:09:19.481 --> 00:09:22.421
since having kids, you're so concerned

00:09:22.421 --> 00:09:25.389
about all this other stuff,
what other people think of you,

00:09:25.389 --> 00:09:27.183
and how other people are seeing you,

00:09:27.183 --> 00:09:30.089
is kind of your last priority as a parent

00:09:30.089 --> 00:09:31.942
but being at the Getty,
wearing that ridiculous

00:09:31.942 --> 00:09:35.588
outfit, having everybody
staring at me, was fine.

00:09:35.588 --> 00:09:37.019
I mean, I had to keep reminding myself

00:09:37.019 --> 00:09:38.413
that I was wearing something weird,

00:09:38.413 --> 00:09:39.483
and that's why everyone was looking,

00:09:39.483 --> 00:09:42.204
because I didn't even
notice and I did not care.

00:09:42.204 --> 00:09:43.684
So if you are a parent and you're not

00:09:43.684 --> 00:09:45.873
feeling the most confident, have your kid

00:09:45.873 --> 00:09:47.809
dress you for a day, go out in public,

00:09:47.809 --> 00:09:49.922
and just be like, "Screw you, everybody,

00:09:49.922 --> 00:09:51.879
"this is what I'm wearing and I'm happy."

00:09:51.879 --> 00:09:53.143
So that's all I got for today.

00:09:53.143 --> 00:09:55.300
I'm Hannah and I absolutely loved

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:57.235
trying this, I loved this idea.

00:09:57.235 --> 00:09:59.207
I love hearing what you guys wanna see

00:09:59.207 --> 00:10:01.954
so please send me more
ideas, leave them in the

00:10:01.954 --> 00:10:05.313
comments or text me,
this is a real number.

00:10:05.313 --> 00:10:07.220
I read every text, I
don't reply to all of them

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:08.975
because I get a lot, but I do read

00:10:08.975 --> 00:10:10.535
every text that you guys send,

00:10:10.535 --> 00:10:12.918
and I love hearing what
you guys wanna see.

00:10:12.918 --> 00:10:14.245
Now, if you'll excuse me, I'm gonna go

00:10:14.245 --> 00:10:16.887
change into sweatpants and a t-shirt.

00:10:16.887 --> 00:10:20.749
(laughs) 'Cause that's me.
'Til next time!

00:10:20.749 --> 00:10:22.585
Can you smile, Wyatt?

00:10:22.585 --> 00:10:25.459
(gentle jazzy music)

00:10:25.459 --> 00:10:28.209
Oh yeah, you have the best smile.

